{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO/JCO no-fault eviction relocation assistance","requirement":"For no-fault evictions of RSO- or JCO-covered units, a landlord must file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD before serving notice and pay relocation assistance within 15 days of service.","key_value":"$11,000–$27,400 per unit (July 1, 2026–June 30, 2027)","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance or the Just Cause Ordinance displaced by a no-fault eviction; amounts turn on tenancy length and tenant age, disability, family status or income.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"RSO- or JCO-covered rental units in Los Angeles"},"exemptions":"Replacing a resident manager; hazardous conditions from a natural disaster not caused by landlord negligence; offset of accrued rent against relocation assistance; single-family dwellings owned by natural persons with no more than four units receive one month's rent; Mom and Pop reduced payments for owner or relative occupancy.","penalty":"Failure to file the Declaration makes the eviction a violation of the RSO or JCO; a tenant may raise non-payment as an affirmative defense or file a complaint with LAHD.","effective_date":"2026-07-01","citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 151.09","quoted_span":"All tenant not- at-fault evictions require payment of relocation assistance and the filing of a Declaration of Intent to Evict form with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) before evicting tenants from units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","interaction":"Relocation amounts are the minimum; the State Housing Crisis Act or the City RPO may require higher payments for lower income tenants.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":true,"conflict_note":"Bulletin A requires the notice copy to be filed with LAHD within 3 days, while Bulletin B says within 3 business days."}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance demolition relocation","requirement":"Before demolishing a Protected Unit for new construction, an owner must file a Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD, give tenants a 6-month notice, and pay the highest applicable state or City relocation amount.","key_value":"$250,000 per displaced unit (minimum penalty)","coverage_conditions":"Owners demolishing Protected Units for new construction within 5 years of filing the Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict in Los Angeles.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Protected Units demolished for new construction"},"exemptions":"Regular RSO or JCO relocation rules apply if the units to be demolished are not Protected Units or are not occupied by a lower income tenant.","penalty":"Financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","effective_date":"2025-02-11","citation":"L.A. Ordinance Nos. 188481, 188482","quoted_span":"Failure to comply with the RPO may result in financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","interaction":"Owner must pay the higher of State Housing Crisis Act or City RSO/JCO relocation amounts.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Housing Crisis Act demolition relocation for lower income households","requirement":"When lower income households (80% AMI or lower) are displaced by demolition of their units for new construction, the owner must pay relocation benefits consistent with those public entities pay under Government Code Chapter 16.","key_value":"80% AMI or lower","coverage_conditions":"Lower income households, at or below 80 percent of Area Median Income, displaced by demolition of their units where the owner will replace the units with new construction.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"demolition for new construction displacing lower income households"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Gov. Code § 66300.6","quoted_span":"The City’s Resident Protections Ordinance (RPO) and the State’s Housing Crisis Act (HCA) require that ONLY lower income households (80% AMI or lower) being displaced for demolition of their units where the owner will replace the units with new construction receive relocation payment consistent to the relocation benefits required to be paid by public entities under Chapter 16 (commencing with Section 7260) of Division 7 of Title 1 (Government Code 66300.6(b)(4)(A)).","interaction":"City RSO/JCO relocation amounts are the minimum; HCA may require an increase for lower income tenants.","confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
